DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Interval");

Context("Vector");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{8, 13} U {8, 13} U [6, infinity) U ([6, infinity) U {7, 12} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {8, 13}))");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("([6, infinity) - {7, 12})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(3, 6) U (3, 6) U (1, 10)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((3, 6)) U (3, 6) U ((1, 10)) U (3, 6)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("((1, 10)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (3, 6)) U (3, 6)");
BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 3 < x < 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 < x < 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(A) \cup A \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(B) \cap A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

What is the value of [`12+17-2-12/14`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(26.1428571429),width=>1}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{7, 12\}`]
- [`B = \{8, 13\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup B \cup C \cup (C \cup A \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`C - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
